  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Daylight Studio Binder",
    "overview": "NOVA Studio feels like a working binder opened on a bright desk: a quiet neutral navigation rail, a white working sheet, pale citron project context, and compact olive notation. The workspace is the visual material. Real task controls and reconciled counts establish its character before any product explanation.\n\nKeep the mood calm, precise, and approachable. Stack Sans gives headings a little personality while dense text, native selectors, restrained icons, and clear alignment keep work readable. The user explicitly rejected the prior cobalt marketing interface and its resemblance to Forge; this active world replaces that marketing composition with a complete workspace.",
